 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch07_04_02\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id1807698\" data-alt=\"This illustration shows an ATP synthase enzyme embedded in the inner mitochondrial membrane. ATP synthase allows protons to move from an area of high concentration in the intermembrane space to an area of low concentration in the mitochondrial matrix. The energy derived from this exergonic process is used to synthesize ATP from ADP and inorganic phosphate.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20240910.161227/resources/3266f7f79ef9149d89113dced736731f46bf456b\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"This illustration shows an ATP synthase enzyme embedded in the inner mitochondrial membrane. ATP synthase allows protons to move from an area of high concentration in the intermembrane space to an area of low concentration in the mitochondrial matrix. The energy derived from this exergonic process is used to synthesize ATP from ADP and inorganic phosphate.\" width=\"320\" height=\"392\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 503366,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Dinitrophenol (DNP) is an uncoupler that makes the inner mitochondrial membrane leak protons <span data-math=\"(\\text{H}^{+} {\\!})\">(\\text{H}^{+} {\\!})</span>. It was used until 1938 as a weight-loss drug. Why do you think this might be an effective weight-loss drug?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 989447,
     "content_html": "DNP dissipates the proton gradient in the matrix, preventing the production of ATP. The body then increases its metabolic rate, leading to weight loss."
    },
    {
     "id": 989448,
     "content_html": "DNP decreases the proton gradient in the inner mitochondrial space, leading to rapid consumption of acetyl-CoA, which causes weight loss."
    },
    {
     "id": 989449,
     "content_html": "DNP blocks the movement of protons through the ATP synthase, halting ATP production. The stored energy dissipates as heat, causing weight loss."
    },
    {
     "id": 989450,
     "content_html": "DNP uncouples the production of ATP by increasing the proton gradient in the matrix. The stored energy dissipates as heat, causing weight loss."
    }
   ],
